ROUTED FINDING — a second defect in a file you already own, not in the audit register.

While planning sibling task-6a31a86fdcd84795a8fae6e5d6978d2c (persistFileDurably short write) I found the IDENTICAL defect in this task's file. Measured at HEAD 192360e:

packages/store/src/backup-generation.ts:37-46
```
async function persistFile(path: string, payload: Uint8Array): Promise<void> {
  await mkdir(dirname(path), { recursive: true });
  const handle = await open(path, "w");
  try {
    await handle.write(payload);     // <-- bytesWritten never checked
    await handle.sync();
  } finally {
    await handle.close();
  }
}
```

FileHandle.write resolves with {bytesWritten, buffer} and may write fewer bytes than requested. The return type is Promise<void>, so a partial write is indistinguishable from a complete one. This is byte-for-byte the same body as recovery-anchor-fs.ts:23-31, which the audit DID record as item 3 — the register named only one of the two copies.

Why it lands on you rather than on the sibling task: backup-generation.ts is YOUR owned path. Two tasks editing one file in this shared worktree is exactly the collision the epic rails warn about, so I did not widen the sibling task to reach in here.

Why it matters for your task specifically: persistFile is what writes the staged manifest at backup-generation.ts:168-171, immediately before the publish you are making crash-safe. A truncated manifest written there would be renamed into finalPath by your new publish path and then pass the post-rename fsync — your atomicity work would faithfully publish truncated bytes. Fixing the publish window without this leaves a hole in the same sequence.

Suggested handling: fix it inside your task and note it in your completion, or decline it in writing so it is not silently dropped. The sibling task's plan carries the matching fix for recovery-anchor-fs.ts, including the sharp part — sync() must run only AFTER the payload is fully written, since a sync between partial writes flushes a truncated file and produces false durable evidence while looking more careful than the original.

Not blocking your plan; the approved plan stands. This is one extra line to fix in a function you are already reading.
